{"path":"thread/promise/set_exception","title":"std::promise<R>::set_exception","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::promise&lt;R&gt;::</span>set_exception","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/promise/set_exception","section":"thread","kind":"page","summary":"Atomically stores the exception pointer p into the shared state and makes the state ready.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> set_exception<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception_ptr\"><span class=\"kw780\">std::<span class=\"me2\">exception_ptr</span></span></a> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Atomically stores the exception pointer <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> into the shared state and makes the state ready. \n</p><p>The operation behaves as though <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise/set_value\">set_value</a></span>, <code>set_exception</code>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise/set_value_at_thread_exit\">set_value_at_thread_exit</a></span>, and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise/set_exception_at_thread_exit\">set_exception_at_thread_exit</a></span> acquire a single mutex associated with the promise object while updating the promise object.\n</p><p>An exception is thrown if there is no shared state or the shared state already stores a value or exception.\n</p><p>Calls to this function do not introduce data races with calls to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise/get_future\">get_future</a></span> (therefore they need not synchronize with each other).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> exception pointer to store. The behavior is undefined if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> is null\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_error\">std::future_error</a></span> on the following conditions:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> has no shared state. The error code is set to <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_errc\"><code>no_state</code></a>.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li> The shared state already stores a value or exception. The error code is set to <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_errc\"><code>promise_already_satisfied</code></a>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;future&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;thread&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise\"><span class=\"kw2200\">std::<span class=\"me2\">promise</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> p<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future\"><span class=\"kw2201\">std::<span class=\"me2\">future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> f <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> p.<span class=\"me1\">get_future</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/thread\"><span class=\"kw2167\">std::<span class=\"me2\">thread</span></span></a> t<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>p<span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"co1\">// code that may throw</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">throw</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/runtime_error\"><span class=\"kw774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">runtime_error</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Example\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n                <span class=\"co1\">// store anything thrown in the promise</span>\n                p.<span class=\"me1\">set_exception</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/current_exception\"><span class=\"kw782\">std::<span class=\"me2\">current_exception</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <span class=\"co1\">// or throw a custom exception instead</span>\n                <span class=\"co1\">// p.set_exception(std::make_exception_ptr(MyException(\"mine\")));</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"co1\">// set_exception() may throw too</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> f.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception\"><span class=\"kw768\">std::<span class=\"me2\">exception</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> e<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Exception from the thread: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    t.<span class=\"me1\">join</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Exception from the thread: Example</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise/set_exception_at_thread_exit\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>set_exception_at_thread_exit</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  sets the result to indicate an exception while delivering the notification only at thread exit <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/promise","title":"std::promise"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::promise<R>::set_exception","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Atomically stores the exception pointer p into the shared state and makes the state ready."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"std::future_error on the following conditions:"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"set_exception_at_thread_exit","note":"sets the result to indicate an exception while delivering the notification only at thread exit"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":253,"codeBlockCount":2}
